From 5dfeb4443a367b2f050f902210aa149246deb409 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 07:58:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 058/167] iio: adc: Add MediaTek MT6720 charger ADC and fuel
 gauge AUXADC

The charger ADC converts one channel at a time: the channel number goes
to 0x14f, which reads back non-zero until the conversion is done, then
to the report select in 0x155, and the result is read big-endian from
0x156. Results are in mV and mA; the junction temperature is in degrees
C offset by 64. This is the sequence of MediaTek's mt6720-adc driver.

The fuel gauge AUXADC has its own trigger register (0x938, one bit per
channel). Each channel's data has a ready bit on top: the battery
voltage (15 bits of 7.36 V full scale), the thermistor and its
reference (12 bits of 2.76 V), as MediaTek's mt6375-auxadc driver reads
them for the MT6720.

Consumers name a charger ADC channel by its hardware number.
